# Session Connect requires protocol-surface proof (hard rule)

Operator defect (2026-08-05): Playwright reported large PASS matrices
(nav, PAM crawl, live-session binder 22/22, admin) while **My Workstations
/ Connect never opened a real VDI or interactive session**. Chrome-only
asserts, options HTTP 200, Jump fleet page load, and mocked workstation
lists were treated as “Connect works.” RCA:
`pim-offline-server/docs/dev/connect-qa-failure-rca-20260805.md`.

## The rule

> **Never claim Connect, Open, Launch, VDI, live session, or interactive
> desktop/SSH “works,” “fixed,” or “PASS” unless Playwright (or an
> inspected screenshot) proves the protocol surface: canvas, iframe, or
> xterm showing status `connecting` or `connected`, with a non-zero,
> non-nil session id — against at least one named live lab seat (Lab
> Docker Linux PAM PAW / `pimadmin` or an equivalent documented seat).**

This rule is **stricter** than
[`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc)
for PAM / session paths. Layout visibility and bounding-box proof remain
required; they are **not** Connect acceptance.

## What counts as protocol-surface proof

All of the following must hold in one evidence artifact (e2e assert and/or
inspected screenshot + network notes):

| Requirement | Pass condition |
| --- | --- |
| Session id | From Open/Connect URL or JSON; UUID; **not** empty, **not** `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000` |
| Protocol surface | Visible `.xterm` / `canvas` / session iframe (e.g. `live-ssh-terminal`, `live-vnc-canvas`) |
| Status | Chip/text matches `/connecting|connected/i` (not merely “page loaded”) |
| Lab seat | Named live target — prefer **Lab Docker Linux PAM PAW**; document equivalent if another seat is used |
| Auth path | Real Open path (WA token when mandatory); HTTP 200 + `decision=denied` / empty `session_id` is **FAIL** |

Canonical e2e pattern:
`pim-offline-server/ui/e2e/my-workstations-connect-paw-embedded-live.spec.ts`.

## Forbidden “false green” acceptance

Do **not** treat any of these alone as Connect / session success:

- Connect / Open / Launch **button visible** or geometry PASS
- Jump fleet / Session Control / Connection points **chrome** or page load
- `GET …/live-sessions/{id}/options` HTTP 200
- Zero-GUID `/options` gate alone (necessary, not sufficient)
- Wake-before-connect / power / drained-Jump infra fixes without a follow-on protocol-surface row
- Mocked `GET /api/enclave/me/workstations` chrome specs (e.g.
  `my-workstations-connect-chrome-embedded-live.spec.ts`)
- Direct navigation to a live route **without** proving the operator
  Connect/Open control path when the claim is about that control
- API Open success for a different seat than the one named in the claim

Label chrome-only specs explicitly as chrome-only in titles and matrix
rows. Never cite them in DONE checklists as “Connect works.”

## Required agent behavior

1. When claiming Connect/Open/Launch/VDI/session fixed: name the e2e file
   (or screenshot path) that proved protocol surface + session id + seat.
2. After reboot/stall or Jump capacity changes: re-run a protocol-surface
   spec before declaring lab Connect healthy.
3. Keep `aic-server-service` Running unless the operator asked for a
   recycle; never use `phil` as a rotation/Connect identity; no `cargo clean`.
4. Cross-link this rule when updating
   [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc)
   or PAM e2e matrices.
5. Comprehensive / multi-protocol claims also require
   [`workstation-protocols-and-command-restrictions.mdc`](workstation-protocols-and-command-restrictions.mdc)
   (SSH **and** RDP **and** VNC when lab seats offer them; workstation-type
   inventory; live command-restriction allow/deny — not SSH-only).

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** Matrix “Live session 22/22 PASS” from binder tabs + Jump
chrome + TightVNC options toolbar, while My Workstations Connect to Docker
PAM PAW never minted WA, never got a real `session_id`, and never showed xterm.

**Fix:** Assert Connect → acknowledge → `/pam/live/ssh/{uuid}` (non-zero),
`live-ssh-terminal` + xterm visible, status `connecting|connected`, evidence
under `docs/dev/evidence/my-workstations-connect-*`. Chrome specs stay
chrome-only.

